        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5dd5c4aa-dd2e-5dc4-8a15-8160ab5da75c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer, A Charlie Brown Christmas\n- Companies: Rankin/Bass Productions, Universal Television, NBC, CBS, General Electric, Bell Canada\n- People: Johnny Marks, Robert L. May, Lee Mendelson, Bill Melendez, Larry D. Mann\n- Concepts: stop motion animation, television specials, Christmas programming\n\nFacts:\n- In 1939, Robert L. May wrote the poem \"Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer.\"\n- Johnny Marks later based his song \"Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer\" on Robert L. May's 1939 poem of the same name.\n- Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer is a 1964 Christmas stop motion animated television special produced by Rankin/Bass Productions and currently distributed by Universal Television.\n- Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer first aired in the United States on NBC on Sunday, December 6, 1964.\n- General Electric sponsored Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer under the umbrella title \"The General Electric Fantasy Hour.\"\n- A Charlie Brown Christmas was produced by Lee Mendelson, directed by Bill Melendez, and debuted on CBS on December 9, 1965.\n- Larry D. Mann voiced Yukon Cornelius in Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer.\n- In the 1980s, Larry D. Mann was best known as \"The Boss\" in a series of Bell Canada television commercials.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7e5eeabf-37f4-5c69-a333-4c702a6c6148",
        "text": "Page: Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer (TV special). Sentence: Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer is a 1964 Christmas stop motion animated television special produced by Rankin/Bass Productions and currently distributed by Universal Television.\nPage: Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer (TV special). Sentence: It first aired Sunday, December 6, 1964, on the NBC television network in the United States, and was sponsored by General Electric under the umbrella title of \"The General Electric Fantasy Hour\".\nPage: Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer (TV special). Sentence: The special was based on the Johnny Marks song \"Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer\" which was itself based on the poem of the same name written in 1939 by Marks' brother-in-law, Robert L. May.\nPage: A Charlie Brown Christmas. Sentence: Produced by Lee Mendelson and directed by Bill Melendez, the program made its debut on CBS on December 9, 1965.\nPage: Larry D. Mann. Sentence: He was best known as \"The Boss\" in a series of Bell Canada television commercials in the 1980s and for voicing the character of Yukon Cornelius in \"Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer\".",
